A||N||11||Monkeyman||Remote decklid release won't work||||5||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||11-24-2001||06:51 PM||||Tried it tonight and all I got was a dimly glowing brake light (on the dash).  All I've done to the car since I know it worked was remove the 3<sup>rd</sup> brake light and remove the drivers side headlight motor (awaiting Rodneys new gear).  I tried pulling the E brake up but that didn't work, either.  What gives?  I've never had this happen before.  In the past, either it worked or it didn't, but no glowing brake/idiot light.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/patriot.gif">    <BR><B><FONT COLOR="red">Proud</FONT> <FONT COLOR="white">to be an</FONT> <FONT COLOR="blue">American</FONT>!!</B>||||reg||5
Z||000001||watts||11-24-2001||07:25 PM||||Keep in mind that the trunk release grounds itself through the actual latch 'loop' itself.  Make sure it hasn't got really grunged.<P>Poke a test light or meter into the appropriate wire of the 3 terminal connector at the front right of the engine compartment going up to the latch, and have a helper hit the button.  If it lights up, you're most of the way there.  If not, check the fuse, and check the trunk relay.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Max The Chainsaw||11-24-2001||07:39 PM||||Definatly a ground. The latch can't find a path to ground so it's finding one thru the dash light bulb. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||11-25-2001||08:06 AM||||Where would I look for a bad ground?  As I said, the only thing I've done to the car since I knew this was working was to remove the left headlight motor.  Could this have anything to do with it?  I'd hate to have to reinstall the motor just to see if this is the problem.||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroBUZZ||11-25-2001||08:16 AM||||MM:   Mine started doing EXACTLY the same thing the other day.  Skitime and Phi figured it was a ground or the relay but I haven't gone snooping yet.  Let me know if you find a cure, please.<BR>Gary<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||11-25-2001||12:56 PM||||Where's the relay?  And can you (or anyone) lead me to where a grounding problem might lie?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||11-25-2001||07:05 PM||||I looked and looked for a problem and found none (at least not in the places I looked).  I tried plugging headlight motor back in, but that didn't cure the problem, either.  I did find that if I pull the E brake up, the brake idiot light doesn't come on anymore.  Wonder why this didn't work this way yesterday?  I could really use some more help as I can't afford to take it to the shop right now.  I'm still trying to pay off my last bill with them.||||reg||1
Z||000007||SCCA FIERO||11-25-2001||07:24 PM||||There is a switch on the E-brake handle. Mine did this as well, but no brake light lit up. Pull back the carpet near the e-brake and check the switch. Mine was plugged in but the metal thing on the switch wasn't contacting the e-brake lever.<P>Or try locating the wires as the run out of the decklid (if you can open it) and make sure they are plugged in.<P>Or Maybe the switch is bad. Jump the terminals to see if it works. Not sure which ones to jump, but I tried all of them to find the right ones. I know I jumped the wrong ones at some point, but it all still works.<P>Just a few things to check, maybe it will be of some help   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by SCCA FIERO (edited 11-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||SCCA FIERO||11-25-2001||07:28 PM||||Just reread everything. I would guess it's the switch on the e-brake lever itself.<P>The relay is located on the steering column under the dash, on the right hand side. It's mounted in this metal bracket that kind of captures it like a claw. You can test this relay by replacing it with the horn relay (located by the blue dingy thingy). If it still doesn't work, it's the e-brake switch.<P>But my money is on the e-brake switch. I bet you did something to it when you removed the third brake light.<P>BTW, why did you remove the third brake light?||||reg||1
Z||000009||Monkeyman||11-25-2001||07:39 PM||||I'll check the E brake lever tomorrow after work.  Thanx for the tip.<P>I got rid of my 3<sup>rd</sup> brake light because of visibility problems to the rear.  I have to have the mirror adjusted just so and that means that most of what I saw was the brake light.||||reg||1
Z||000010||ka4nkf||11-25-2001||11:47 PM||||Raise The Trunk Lid And Put A Jumper From The Engine And To The Trunk Latch. If It Does Not Work Now Then It Is Not The Ground.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Mr.Frosty||11-26-2001||12:15 AM||||Mine is doing that,and I pulled the relay.I figured the relay was bad.I found it by hitting the switch and following the clinkety clank sound that was coming from it.When I hit the switch,the relay would make a tinny clank.Does that mean the relay is bad, or is it the solenoid that is bad,and the relay is doing it's job? I think it's the first one,because the relay's not supposed to pop like that.<P>------------------<BR>85 GT Turbo intercooled||||reg||1
